From: WXbet <57314510+WXbet@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] process/v2/exit_code: guard static_asserts on MIPS

boost/process/v2/exit_code.hpp guards its still_active constant with
four static_assert calls on WIFSTOPPED / WIFEXITED / WIFSIGNALED /
WIFCONTINUED. These fail to compile on MIPS with

  error: non-constant condition for static assertion
  error: call to non-'constexpr' function 'int __WIFSTOPPED(int)'

whenever env.cpp (or any other TU pulling exit_code.hpp) is compiled.

Root cause: glibc 2.44 added a MIPS-specific
sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/mips/bits/waitstatus.h (introduced by commit
c19cdbf66ff62a4578ac2117d43ebb306ae36aeb, prior releases used the
generic macro-based header on MIPS as well). The new file defines
__WIFSTOPPED and __WIFSIGNALED as `static inline int` functions rather
than macros so that MIPS's SIGRTMAX=127 special-case (status 0x7f)
can be handled correctly. Those inline functions are not constexpr,
so the static_asserts cannot evaluate them.

The asserts are compile-time sanity checks on Boost's own still_active
constant (0x17f); the semantics on MIPS are unchanged (WIFSTOPPED
returns true, the other three return false, as intended). Guard the
block with `#ifndef __mips__` so the checks keep firing on every port
where they can, and are skipped only on the arch where glibc has
implemented the underlying primitives as inline functions.

Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/boostorg/process/pull/565]

Signed-off-by: WXbet <57314510+WXbet@users.noreply.github.com>

--- a/boost/process/v2/exit_code.hpp	2026-08-01 12:33:51.628201500 +0200
+++ b/boost/process/v2/exit_code.hpp	2026-08-01 14:26:21.823659200 +0200
@@ -73,10 +73,18 @@
 namespace detail
 {
 constexpr native_exit_code_type still_active = 0x17f;
+// glibc 2.44 introduced sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/mips/bits/waitstatus.h
+// which defines WIFSTOPPED and WIFSIGNALED as non-constexpr `static
+// inline int` functions instead of macros, so that MIPS's SIGRTMAX=127
+// special-case (status 0x7f) can be handled. Earlier glibc used the
+// generic macro-based header on MIPS too. Skip the compile-time
+// sanity checks on the one arch where they can no longer compile.
+#ifndef __mips__
 static_assert(WIFSTOPPED(still_active), "Expected still_active to indicate WIFSTOPPED");
 static_assert(!WIFEXITED(still_active), "Expected still_active to not indicate WIFEXITED");
 static_assert(!WIFSIGNALED(still_active), "Expected still_active to not indicate WIFSIGNALED");
 static_assert(!WIFCONTINUED(still_active), "Expected still_active to not indicate WIFCONTINUED");
+#endif
 }
 
 inline bool process_is_running(int code)
